Why 6b, and why exactly this tarball
------------------------------------
Read out of the executable, not guessed. jerror.c's JMESSAGE table lives at
VA 0x00754B90 in HitmanBloodMoney.exe:
    [73] "Copyright (C) 1998, Thomas G. Lane"    (JMSG_COPYRIGHT)
    [74] "6b  27-Mar-1998"                       (JMSG_VERSION)
Both strings are reproduced character-for-character by this tarball's
jversion.h -- including the DOUBLE SPACE in "6b  27-Mar-1998".

The table's size is a second, independent check. Upstream jerror.h expands to
exactly 124 JMESSAGE entries (codes 0..123), so the last message code is
123 = 0x7B -- which is precisely the 0x7B the game's jpeg_std_error hard-codes.

Ruling out neighbours:
  - "Sorry, there are legal restrictions on arithmetic coding" IS present in
    the exe, and IS present here; libjpeg 7 removed it, so 7/8/9 are out.
  - None of the 7/8 additions ("Invalid crop request", DCT-scaling messages)
    appear in the exe.
  - 6a would read "Copyright (C) 1996".
  - libjpeg-turbo post-dates this 2006 build.
So: 6b exactly, unmodified.

Module provenance
-----------------
The only RCS ident string in the whole 4.3MB image (.rdata 0x354478) is:
    $Header: /var/lib/cvs/code/libraries/jpegdll/cactusjpeg.c,v 1.3
             2003/11/10 18:47:08 st Exp $
That attests IOI's module directory: code/libraries/jpegdll/ -- which is why
our transcriptions live at src/libraries/jpegdll/ (source root is z:\code\;
hmcd_dbg.map shows only two top-level dirs, jamout_hitman3 and libraries).

libjpeg is PC-only. The PS2 build contains no libjpeg at all (0 case-insensitive
hits for "jpeg" across all 167MB of hmcd_dbg.elf, STABS included), so there is
no PS2 source_file mapping to inherit. The iOS Reprisal port DOES link libjpeg,
but only the COMPRESS half (jinit_c_*, jpeg_CreateCompress, jpeg_write_scanlines,
jpeg_fdct_*, ... 47 symbols) -- useful as a naming source for that half only.

Traps when byte-matching this band
----------------------------------
The original was linked with /OPT:ICF, so identical bodies were folded to one
RVA. Five folded export RVAs (each is ONE function in the image -- do not chase
both halves as separate byte-matches):
    0x0000FCF0  jpeg_destroy_compress == jpeg_destroy_decompress
    0x0000FD00  jpeg_abort_compress   == jpeg_abort_decompress
    0x000236A0  jpeg_get_small        == jpeg_get_large
    0x000236B0  jpeg_free_small       == jpeg_free_large
    0x000715C0  jpeg_mem_term         == EditPrint   (<- NOT libjpeg)
Three more folded into unrelated game code, so those RVAs are not libjpeg's to
own: 0x000715C0 (EditPrint), 0x002B3640 (jpeg_mem_init), 0x0003BAE0 (jzero_far).

Also: d3dx9_27.dll ships Microsoft's own copy of libjpeg 6b with identical
version/copyright strings. It is unrelated to the game's copy.

Scope
-----
Reference and diff base only -- NOTHING here is compiled. The build inputs are
